{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '569,639p' review-inputs/1793650000000-architect-6d-plan-v2.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"#### 6d-b: holder, custody, expiry, recovery\n\n**Change.**\n1. `driver.cljc` `run-cycle` (`:2111-2144`): `:fuel` config key (checked in `check-common!` `:177-207`, positive integer or nil); `(if fuel (sr/run-fuel m0 fuel) (vm/run m0))` under the existing gate and halted guards; **each stage's machine assoc'd into the state before the next tenure check**; `cycle-result` adds `:yin.k/at-boundary true`; `step-active`'s catch ends the run on the state it was handed and records `:yin.k/retained-boundary`; `end-run` keeps the retained machine on the ended state (gated `:ended`, never offered).\n2. `export.cljc`: `kind-of` (`:274-282`) `:running` first; `enter` (`:121-149`) drops `first-refusal` and moves the ready queue into the record (`:ready []` on the machine; `:yin.k/recovery-ready` on fenced restore); `recovery-metadata`/`valid-state?` count ready entries; `abort` unchanged (its conditions are right).\n3. `semantic.cljc` `vm-hot` entry gate guard (§3.3 outcome 4); `run-fuel` inherits it.\n4. `ledger.cljc:277`, `authority/grant.cljc:74-75`: admit `:running`.\n5. Docstrings per §3.8 (driver, compose, export header).\n6. Tests: `driver_test`: a fuelled run preempts a long pure loop at a boundary, the phase stays `:running`, the next tick continues; `hand-off` mints, journals, freezes and offers a `:running` pack; a candidate lowers it (awaiting-grant → grant → `activate`) and reaches the reference result; the five clock-controlled cuts of §3.3 with their assertions; `rehydrate-fenced` byte equality for a running root with a wait and with a ready entry, and the rehydrated machine refuses `vm/step` (\"Gate is closed\"); two competing candidates; stale-source stepping refused; uncertain-offer abort refused; expired-grant admission refused; a halted exclusive root still restores without a grant (F6 regression). `ledger_test`/`grant_test`: a `:running` baseline is offerable; `:halted` is not. `compose_rows_test`: an exclusive world handed off at a boundary completes on the successor; one with a running install child. `stage_e_scenarios`: `[:until \"h1\" :running n] [:hand-off \"h1\"]` with fuel so the hand-off lands mid-body; recovery cut before and after the offer; a tenure-expiry cut between slices asserting the last checkpoint is what recovers.\n7. Docs: §3.7.1 §7.3; §3.7.3 UCF §7.7.4, §7.7.6, §7.8, §7.10, §7.11, §7.11.1, `:2842`; §3.7.6.\n\n**Depends on.** 6d-a. **Days.** 2.5 + 1.5 (3 rounds) = 4.\n\n#### 6e: the cross-engine half\n\n**Change.** `layout.cljc`: `lift-running`/`lower-running` over the kernels' live fields (register `{:pc :registers :frames :continuation :store-of}`, stack `{:pc :stack :frames :continuation :store-of}`); `virt` over a given virtual set (`L(p)` for a run); `register-window` parameterised; nil fill outside `L(p)`; `h->a` relabels `:push`; `slice-window`/`lift-stack` dead-prefix rule (`≥`, prefix dropped, diagnostic); `lower-stack`/`stack-k` unchanged in shape; `safepoint!` run mode (any pc inside a body); `canonical-task` lifts an active kernel as `:running` (with waits and ready as the semantic lift does; backends still refuse installs); `kernel-task` lowers a `:running` machine into a running kernel. No kernel edit. `layout_test`, the harness: laws 4 and 5 at every aligned boundary on the 61 lane cases.\n\n**Acceptance.** Law 4: one root id on three lanes at aligned boundary `i` (stack index after `:push` relabelling), taken and untaken branches both pinned, ordered operand multiplicity pinned; law 5: six ordered pairs at every boundary, each continuing to the reference result, with the **full-payload refusal oracle** of §3.6 (exact refusals and exact successful transfers per case and direction); the `:push` relabelling pinned on one row; **item 6, tail residuals**: either a lane-fragment case with a non-empty ambient layout at a tail call exercises the dead-prefix rule (lift drops, lower omits, law 1 and law 4 hold, the diagnostic reports the count) or the static check `layout(p) = []` at every tail-call pc of the fragment proves none exists and the rule is pinned on a hand-built vector; `layout-refusals` rewritten: a kernel stepped to a non-parking pc lifts on both lanes with zero serves refused; a hand-built entry outside every body refuses `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; the fragment is not widened (rows 7-12 and 17 excluded; row 4 not lowered).\n\n**Depends on.** 6d-a; independent of 6d-b. **Days.** 3.5 + 1.5 (3 rounds) = 5.\n\n#### Effort\n\n| Slice | Implementation days | Review rounds | Days |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6d-a reference lane, grammar, fuel, static layouts | 3 | 3 | 4.5 |\n| 6d-b holder, custody, expiry, recovery | 2.5 | 3 | 4 |\n| 6e cross-engine | 3.5 | 3 | 5 |\n| docs (§3.7, §3.8), split across the three | 1.5 | 1 | 1.5 |\n| **Total** | **10.5** | | **15**, or 10 without 6e |\n\nWhat the review said to keep: targeted counterexamples (F1, F2, F5 states), the all-pc static gates, the quick structural sample, one full three-host run at landing, every custody race and scheduler product. What may be cut during iteration: repetitive broad end-to-end cases. No wall-time is forecast; the slow tier's duration is measured once at 6d-a landing and recorded in the ledger row.\n\nRouting: codex (gpt-6.1-sol, workspace-write, stdin closed), one brief per slice, foreground lanes only, report inside the worktree's `collab/`; Fable reviews at every gate under the Q6 rule; glm/cmd as non-author fallback; commit only on Architect sign-off; never commit `collab/` or `docs/agents/routing-status.md`.\n\n### 3.10 Decisions for the owner (defaults stated so 6d-a can start)\n\n1. **Task slots 17 (`run`) and 18 (`ready`)**, re-minting every pinned root once right after module-pins commit 2. Alternative: a mixed slot 13 `[:refs :wait :run :ready]`, no re-mint, every slot-13 traversal audited for three row kinds. **Recommend 17/18**: it removes F7's misread class by construction, and the re-mint coincides with one already happening.\n2. **Fuel as a holder config key `:fuel`**, default nil (today's behaviour; nothing changes until a composition opts in). **Recommend as stated.**\n3. **No automatic export at the bound in 6d-b**; `hand-off` stays explicit; `:yin.k/at-boundary` is the signal. A later \"arm when remaining tenure < one renewal interval\" policy belongs in `compose`, needs no VM clock. **Recommend as stated.**\n4. **No adoption of a retained boundary**: an ended holder keeps `:yin.k/retained-boundary` for inspection only; recovery is the last durable checkpoint; the documents state the loss. A future ledger rule \"a regrant to the same holder may continue from its retained boundary when the input prefix and next-op-seq agree\" is possible but is new authority and not in 6d. **Recommend as stated.**\n5. **Q6**: keep edge-reachability liveness; pin the pre-branch `ghost` refusal. A \"no\" means a constant-propagation pass in `live-pcs`, a separate slice. **Recommend keep.**\n6. **Completed `:put` wakes are completed operations**: op-id well-formed, excluded from retained writes and `protect!`, never re-appended. **Recommend as stated** (the alternative, counting them as retained, would make the receiver re-append a datom that is already on the stream).\n7. **`:push` relabelled to its successor**, not refused. **Recommend relabel** (no guest semantics run; the stack content is already its successor's).\n8. **Holds stay refusals** (`:observe`, held, unminted cursor, pending close, link cursor not installed), documented as driver seams mid-step that the driver resolves without guest execution; 6d-b verifies each resolves within one cycle and gives any that does not a known-gaps row. **Recommend as stated.**\n\n### 3.11 Risks\n\n1. **A liveness bug surfaces** at a pc no park looked at: law 1 fails there. A finding, not a slice risk; the main reason to run the every-boundary laws.\n2. **The ready carrier meets a wake reason I did not enumerate** (a link wake entering the queue): pinned as `:ready-reason` refusal in 6d-a and reported; widening is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n3. **Re-mint churn**: two re-mints in a week (module-pins, 6d-a). Mitigation: order (§3.9); 6d's own acceptance pins boundary counts and refusal kinds, never root ids.\n4. **Dead-prefix rule untested on a real case** if the fragment has none: 6e item 6 pins it on a hand-built vector; the rule is then a documented check awaiting a natural case.\n5. **Slow-tier time on Dart**: slow tier only; measured once.\n6. **Gate guard cost**: one map read per `run-fuel`/`vm-hot` call; a reviewer confirms it is outside the loop.\n7. **Fuel too small or too large**: a composition knob; default nil.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification honesty\n\n- Every `file:line` above was read in `7c4dff32` today. The review's citations held in every case I checked; where it cited a function by name I read the body.\n- **Run**: one throwaway JVM test namespace reproducing F1, F2 and F5 (transcript excerpts in §1); deleted; `git status` shows only `collab/`. **Not run**: the harness, the slow tier, any Node or Dart lane, any driver or Stage E scenario, any performance probe. Boundary counts and point counts are to be measured once and pinned by 6d-a.\n- **Claims that are checks** (not theorems): `L(p)` sufficient at every boundary; injectivity over `L(p)` at every pc; the ordered stack equation with the jump/terminator layouts at every pc; the dead-prefix rule; the refusal-oracle equality; cross-host boundary-count equality; the per-tree fuel bound.\n- **Not claimed**: that the de Bruijn kernels reconstruct a `run` state today (6e); that the holder can preempt today (`vm/run` at `driver.cljc:2120`); that fuel bounds wall-clock time; that fuel repairs expiry loss (only exporting before the bound does); that a tail call with a non-empty ambient layout exists in the fragment (6e decides); that link wakes never enter the queue (6d-a verifies by reading `poll-links`); that module-pins commit 2's final hunks are exactly those of `origin/srvm-module-pins` at `62ed14fa` (they are what is merging now).\n- **Timestamps**: the brief dates itself 2026-10-17 21:00 +07 and the owner's ruling 2026-10-17; the machine clock at completion reads 2026-10-16 14:40 +07. The header uses the clock; the ruling's date is quoted as the brief gives it.\n\n## 5. Readiness\n\n**Implementation-ready**: 6d-a, as specified in §3.9, under the defaults of §3.10, **the moment module-pins commit 2 is on master**; its brief can be written now from §3.1, §3.2, §3.4, §3.5 (static part), §3.6, §3.9 and the §3.7 text it owns. 6d-b and 6e are specified to the same level and are ready to brief when 6d-a merges; they run in parallel. **Start first**: 6d-a. The owner's invariant is closed for the holder only when 6d-b lands; the plan says so and does not call it closed earlier.\n\nPLAN-V2-READY\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The consensus permits either shared fuel accounting or a bounded bridge cycle. I’ll use the latter: one execution slice or scheduler round, at most one bridge step, then return. I’m also separating completed outcomes from pending waits so link/install results remain valid after their pending resources are retired.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '45,100p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1010,1148p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '2215,2288p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '250,280p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '280,355p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc; sed -n '310,350p' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc; rg -n 'defn (step|run)|vm-hot|semantic/run' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '45,100p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1010,1148p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '2215,2288p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '250,280p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '280,355p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc; sed -n '310,350p' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc; rg -n 'defn (step|run)|vm-hot|semantic/run' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   :link-response [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D]\n   :install [:S :D]})\n\n\n(def row-table\n  \"Slot descriptors, excluding id and kind. :repeat/:pairs are variadic;\n   :refs is an ordered vector of structural references. :pending is\n   discriminated by pending-table. Nothing in this table is executable.\"\n  {:vec [:repeat :V] :list [:repeat :V] :set [:repeat :V]\n   :map [:pairs :V :V] :bindings [:pairs :S :V] :store [:pairs :D :V]\n   :env [[:ref :bindings] :optional-D]\n   :closure [:A :N :syms [:ref :bindings] :optional-D]\n   :prim [:S] :stream [:D :D] :reified [[:ref :act]] :parked-ref [:D]\n   :act [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] [:ref :k] :N]\n   :tail [:A :N [:ref :k]]\n   :window [:pairs :N :V] :k [:repeat [:ref :kframe]]\n   :kframe [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] :N]\n   :wait [[:ref :act :tail] [:ref :pending]] :pending :pending\n   :module-store [:D [:ref :store]]\n   :parked-table [:pairs :D [:ref :act :tail]]\n   :install [:S :D :D :D [:ref :task]]\n   :cursor-cells [:pairs :C [:ref :cursor-cell-body]] :cursor-cell-body [[:ref :stream] :D]\n   :task [:N :D :D :D :N [:ref :bindings] [:ref :store]\n          [:refs :module-store] [:ref :parked-table] [:ref :cursor-cells]\n          :D :D [:refs :install] [:refs :wait] :optional-D :optional-V :optional-D]})\n\n\n(defn node\n  [kind slots]\n  {:kind kind :slots (if (= :window kind)\n                       (vec (mapcat identity (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))))\n                       (vec slots))})\n\n\n(defn- refuse!\n  [status kind path]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Row codec refused data\"\n                  {:yin.k/status status :yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/path path})))\n\n\n(defn- bad!\n  [kind path]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable kind path))\n\n\n(defn- marker-shaped?\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= 1 (count x)) (or (contains? x :yin.k/row) (contains? x :yin.k/cursor-cell))))\n\n\n(defn- check-literal-markers!\n  [x]\n  (when (marker-shaped? x) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :marker []))\n  (when (coll? x)\n    (doseq [v (if (map? x) (mapcat identity x) x)] (check-literal-markers! v)))\n  (when (meta x) (check-literal-markers! (meta x))))\n\n\n(defn- value-node\n  [x]\n  (check-literal-markers! x)\n  [:lit x])\n\n\n(defn- decoded-value\n  [v]\n  (case (first v)\n    :row {:yin.k/row (second v)}\n    :cursor-cell {:yin.k/cursor-cell (second v)}\n    :lit (if (marker-shaped? (second v)) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :marker []) (second v))))\n\n\n(defn- keyed-node\n  [kind m encode]\n  (node kind (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [k (encode v)]) m)))\n\n\n(defn- env-node\n  [e encode]\n  (node :env [(keyed-node :bindings (:yin.k/bindings e) encode) (:yin.k/store-of e)]))\n\n\n(defn- kframe-node\n  [f encode]\n  (node :kframe [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/pc f) (env-node (:yin.k/env f) encode)\n                 (keyed-node :window (:yin.k/window f) encode) (:yin.k/rd f)]))\n\n\n(def pending-keys\n  {:next [:yin.k/cursor-cell]\n   :put [:yin.k/stream :yin.k/value :yin.k/op-id]\n   :ffi [:yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/call-id :yin.k/op]\n   :ffi-request [:yin.k/call-id :yin.k/envelope :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/response-cursor-cell :yin.k/op-id]\n   :link-request [:yin.k/link-id :yin.k/name :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/envelope :yin.k/op-id :yin.k/try?]\n   :link-response [:yin.k/link-id :yin.k/name :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/try?]\n   :install [:yin.k/name :yin.k/try?]})\n\n\n(defn frame->rows\n  \"Encode a keyed frame to a frame-rooted version-3 row pack. Values are\n   plain literals by default. An explicit value encoder classifies portable\n   references as [:row abstract-row] or [:cursor-cell id], distinct from guest maps.\n   This reshapes; frame/defect owns semantic validity.\"\n  ([f] (frame->rows f value-node))\n  ([f encode]\n   (let [k (node :k (mapv #(kframe-node % encode) (:yin.k/k f)))\n         state (if (= :act (:yin.k/state f))\n                 (node :act [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/pc f) (env-node (:yin.k/env f) encode)\n                             (keyed-node :window (:yin.k/window f) encode) k (get-in f [:yin.k/deliver :yin.k/rd])])\n                 (node :tail [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/site f) k]))\n         pending (:yin.k/pending f)\n         reason (:yin.k/reason pending)\n         root (if (contains? f :yin.k/pending)\n                (node :wait [state (node :pending\n                                         (into [reason]\n                                               (map (fn [key d]\n                                                      (let [x (get pending key)]\n                                                        (if (= :V d) (encode x) x)))\n                                                    (get pending-keys reason) (get pending-table reason))))])\n                state)\n         [id rows] (emit-node root {} {})]\n     (pack id rows))))\n\n\n(defn- decode-keyed\n  [n decode-value]\n  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (decode-value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots n))))\n\n\n(defn- decode-env\n  [n decode-value]\n  (let [[bindings store-of] (:slots n)]\n    (cond-> {:yin.k/bindings (decode-keyed bindings decode-value)}\n      (some? store-of) (assoc :yin.k/store-of store-of))))\n\n\n(defn- decode-kframe\n  [n decode-value]\n  (let [[seg pc e w rd] (:slots n)]\n    {:yin.k/frame-type :return :yin.k/segment seg :yin.k/pc pc\n     :yin.k/env (decode-env e decode-value) :yin.k/window (decode-keyed w decode-value) :yin.k/rd rd}))\n\n\n(defn- decode-frame\n  [n decode-value]\n  (if (= :wait (:kind n))\n    (let [[state pending] (:slots n) [reason & slots] (:slots pending)]\n      (assoc (decode-frame state decode-value) :yin.k/pending\n             (into {:yin.k/reason reason}\n                   (map (fn [key d x] [key (if (= :V d) (decode-value x) x)])\n                        (get pending-keys reason) (get pending-table reason) slots))))\n    (let [act? (= :act (:kind n)) [seg pc e w k rd] (:slots n)\n          k (if act? k e)]\n      (cond-> {:yin.k/state (:kind n) :yin.k/segment seg\n               :yin.k/deliver (if act? {:yin.k/deliver :rd :yin.k/rd rd} {:yin.k/deliver :return})\n               :yin.k/k (mapv #(decode-kframe % decode-value) (:slots k))}\n        act? (assoc :yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/env (decode-env e decode-value) :yin.k/window (decode-keyed w decode-value))\n        (not act?) (assoc :yin.k/site pc)))))\n\n\n(defn rows->frame\n  \"Validate row syntax and hashes, then reshape to the keyed frame.\n   Semantic code/context rules remain frame/defect's responsibility.\n   The default decoder produces in-band row/cursor-cell markers that the default\n   encoder refuses. frame->rows after rows->frame is identity only when\n   both sides are given a classifier for those values.\"\n  ([wire] (rows->frame wire decoded-value))\n  ([wire decode-value] (decode-frame (decode wire) decode-value)))\n\n\n(defn validate-frames\n  \"Carrier step 7, after decode's canonical numbering. Judge each task's\n   X1 first, then waits, parked states, and all reified values. Return the\n   first defect with the abstract row path, or nil.\"\n  [task]\n  (let [slots (:slots task) code-map (nth slots 11)\n        free-env (decode-keyed (nth slots 5) decoded-value)\n        waits (nth slots 13)\n        ffi-ids (into #{} (keep (fn [w]\n                                  (let [[_ p] (:slots w) [reason & xs] (:slots p)]\n                                    (case reason :ffi (second xs) :ffi-request (first xs) nil)))) waits)\n        ctx {:free-env free-env :ffi-call-ids ffi-ids}]\n    (letfn [(judge\n              [n context context-map path]\n              (when-let [d (frame/defect (decode-frame n decoded-value) code-map context context-map)]\n                (-> d (assoc :yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable)\n                    (update :yin.k/path #(into path %)))))\n            (captures\n              [n path]\n              (if (= :reified (:kind n))\n                (or (judge (first (:slots n)) :captured ctx path)\n                    (captures (first (:slots n)) (conj path 0)))\n                (some (fn [[i d x]]\n                        (cond\n                          (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x))) (validate-frames x)\n            (k-of\n              [n]\n              (mapv (fn [f]\n                      (let [[a pc e w rd] (:slots f)]\n                        {:type :return :segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :rd rd}))\n                    (:slots n)))\n            (payload\n              [n]\n              (if (= :tail (:kind n))\n                (let [[a site k] (:slots n)]\n                  {:segment (get aliases a) :site site :k (k-of k) :deliver {:deliver :return}})\n                (let [[a pc e w k rd] (:slots n)]\n                  {:segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :k (k-of k)\n                   :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd rd}})))\n            (parked-record\n              [p]\n              (or (get @cache p)\n                  (do (when (contains? @resolving p)\n                        (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :non-canonicalizable {:yin.k/hint :parked-cycle}))\n                      (swap! resolving conj p)\n                      (let [r (assoc (payload (get parked-index p)) :type :parked-continuation :id p)]\n                        (swap! cache assoc p r)\n                        (swap! resolving disj p)\n                        r))))\n            (cell-stream\n              [c]\n              (stream-key (first (:slots (get bodies c)))))\n            (entry\n              [w]\n              (let [[state pending] (:slots w)\n                    [reason & xs] (:slots pending)\n                    p (payload state)]\n                (case reason\n                  :next (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream (first xs))\n                               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys (first xs))})\n                  :ffi (let [[c call-id op] xs]\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream c) :call-id call-id\n                                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys c)})\n                           (some? op) (assoc :op op)))\n                  :put (let [[s v op-id] xs]\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key s) :datom (value v))\n                           (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  :ffi-request (let [[call-id envelope req resp c op-id] xs\n                                     datom (value envelope)]\n                                 (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key req) :datom datom\n                                                :request-sent true :call-id call-id :op (apply2/request-op datom)\n                                                :response-cursor (get cell-keys c) :response-stream (stream-key resp))\n                                   (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  (:link-request :link-response)\n                  (let [[link-id mn _ _ c] xs\n                        [envelope op-id] (when (= :link-request reason) (drop 5 xs))]\n                    (cond-> (assoc p :reason reason :link-id link-id :name mn\n                                   :request module/link-request-resource :response module/link-response-resource\n                                   :try? (last xs) :cursor (second (:slots (get bodies c))))\n                      (= :link-request reason) (assoc :envelope envelope)\n                      (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  :install (assoc p :reason :install :name (first xs) :try? (second xs)))))]\n      (let [store' (reduce (fn [s [k v]] (engine/store-put s k (value v))) {} (partition 2 (:slots store)))\n            stores (into {} (map (fn [ms]\n                                   (let [[mid s] (:slots ms)]\n                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\n                         module-stores)\n            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\n            entries (mapv entry waits)\n            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\n                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\n                       waits)\n            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\n                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\n                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn (:fenced? custody))]\n                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\n                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\n                                     [base {}] installs)\n            fe (keyed free-env)\n\n(defn restore-initial-env\n  \"After eval, restore :env to initial-env when the computation halted.\n   Blocked and parked states keep the active lexical env for resumption.\"\n  [initial-env result]\n  (if (halted-with-empty-queue? result) (assoc result :env initial-env) result))\n\n\n(defn active-continuation?\n  \"Returns true when the currently active continuation should keep stepping.\"\n  [vm]\n  (and (not (:blocked? vm)) (not (:halted? vm))))\n\n\n(defn ready-for-ingress?\n  \"Returns true when the VM is between evaluations and can accept another\n   program batch: not blocked, nothing scheduled or waiting, no active\n   continuation, and no loaded work.\n\n   This predicate gates observer coordination above the VM. The VM itself\n   never polls a program stream: `step` and `run` execute loaded work only.\"\n  [vm]\n  (let [has-bytecode? (contains? vm :bytecode)\n        bytecode (:bytecode vm)\n        no-bytecode? (and has-bytecode?\n                          (or (nil? bytecode)\n                              (and (sequential? bytecode) (empty? bytecode))))]\n    (and (not (:blocked? vm))\n         (empty? (or (:ready-queue vm) []))\n         (empty? (or (:wait-set vm) []))\n         (nil? (:k vm))\n   stream.\n\n   Returns {:handled? true :vm vm' :request-id id} when a response was\n   appended, or {:handled? false :vm vm ...} otherwise. A `:terminal` key\n   names the outcome that ended the bridge.\"\n  [vm]\n  (let [bridge (:bridge vm)\n        handlers (:handlers bridge)\n        cursor (:cursor bridge)]\n    (cond\n      (:terminal bridge) {:handled? false, :vm vm, :terminal (:terminal bridge)}\n      (:pending-response bridge)\n      (deliver-response vm\n                        (:pending-response bridge)\n                        (:pending-successor bridge)\n                        (:pending-request-id bridge))\n      :else\n      (let [call-in (get (:resources vm) vm/call-in-stream-key)\n            _ (when (nil? call-in)\n                (throw (ex-info \"This VM has no call-in stream to bridge\"\n                                {:bridge? (some? bridge)})))\n            result (stream/next call-in cursor)\n            o (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n        (case o\n          :dao.stream/ok\n          (let [request (:dao.stream/value result)\n                successor (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n                response (apply2/dispatch-request handlers request)]\n            (if (nil? response)\n              ;; A malformed request without a usable id is a local diagnostic\n              ;; and advances once; no handler ever saw it.\n              {:handled? false,\n               :diagnostic :dao.stream.apply/malformed-request,\n               :vm (assoc-in vm [:bridge :cursor] successor)}\n              (deliver-response\n                (telemetry/emit-snapshot\n                  vm\n                  :bridge\n                  {:bridge-op (apply2/request-op request),\n                   :arg-shape (mapv data/tag\n                                    (or (apply2/request-args request) []))})\n                response\n                successor\n                (apply2/request-id request))))\n          :dao.stream/blocked {:handled? false, :vm vm, :outcome o}\n          :dao.stream/gap\n          (throw (ex-info \"Gap at the FFI bridge cursor: a request was evicted and the call that made it can never be answered\"\n                          {:vm-model (:vm-model vm)}))\n          ;; :end, :cursor-mismatch, :invalid-cursor, :transport-error\n          {:handled? false,\n           :terminal o,\n           :vm (assoc-in vm [:bridge :terminal] o)})))))\n\n\n(defn maybe-run\n  \"Run a VM with bridge dispatch if explicit bridge handlers are installed.\n\n   run-fn must be the VM-specific raw runner that advances the VM until halt\n   or block without recursively calling vm/run again.\"\n  [vm run-fn]\n  (if-not (installed? vm)\n    (run-fn vm)\n    (loop [v (run-fn vm)]\n      (if (:blocked? v)\n        (let [{:keys [handled? diagnostic vm]} (bridge-step v)]\n          (cond handled? (recur (run-fn vm))\n                ;; A malformed request consumed as a diagnostic advanced the\n                ;; cursor, so there may be a real request behind it.\n                diagnostic (recur vm)\n                :else vm))\n        v))))\n            :program seg :control {:segment seg :pc 0} :window {} :k nil\n            :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil))))\n\n\n(defn attach-image\n  \"Attach a validated vector without changing execution fields.\"\n  [machine v stamp]\n  (let [image (admit-image machine v stamp {})]\n    (assoc machine :code (store-image (:code machine) image)\n           :code-aliases (store-alias (:code-aliases machine) image))))\n\n\n(defn load-ast\n  \"Project AST datoms through the phase-3 loader.\"\n  [machine datoms stamp]\n  (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n  (load-vector machine (:vector (linearize/project-datoms datoms)) code/contract))\n\n\n(extend-type SemanticVM\n  vm/IVM\n  (step [machine] (telemetry/emit-snapshot\n                    (if (engine/ready-for-ingress? machine) machine (vm-hot machine 1)) :step))\n  (run [machine] (ffi/maybe-run machine register-run-scheduler))\n  (eval [machine ast]\n    (when ast (throw (ex-info \"The semantic VM executes loaded vectors; use load-ast\" {:ast ast})))\n    (engine/restore-initial-env (:env machine) (vm/run machine)))\n  (reset [machine]\n    (assoc machine :control (when-let [seg (:program machine)] {:segment seg :pc 0})\n           :window {} :k nil :value nil :halted? (nil? (:program machine)) :blocked? false))\n  (halted? [machine] (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? machine))\n  (blocked? [machine] (engine/vm-blocked? machine))\n  (value [machine] (engine/vm-value machine))\n  vm/IVMState\n  (control [machine] (:control machine))\n  (environment [machine] (:env machine))\n  (store [machine] (:store machine))\n  (continuation [machine] (:k machine)))\n\n\n(defn create-vm\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
